 "WHAT IS YOUR BIGGEST CHALLENGE IN AUTOMATION?"

Good answer:

Maintaining reliability as the application and execution scale increase. 
The difficulty is usually not writing the first test; it is keeping thousands of automated tests
 deterministic across environments, data and parallel execution. I address that through architecture,
 stable locators, controlled test data, explicit synchronization, isolation, good failure artifacts 
 and regular flaky-test analysis.
 
 
